      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALDEBARAN ZANE (10) saluted two runs back then his luck changed last time when he broke and finished 30 metres back in seventh over 2240m at Melton when sent out as the $2.70 favourite. The driver has some work to do from this wide starting position but meets a similar line up so he is sure to be a force if the manners improve. AFFAIRE DE COVER (7) finished seventh last start over 1609m at this track, beaten 25 metres, after filling a minor placing at the previous appearance over 2300m at this track. Has to contend with a very wide draw. Finds a suitable assignment and can find winning form. LOTUS LOUISE (9) finished fifth last start over 2300m at this track. Generally runs very well at this circuit having won six of his eight wins so can play a big role. CHIEF RUNNINGCLOUD (5) disappointed last time when finishing eighth over 2300m at this track when trying to lead all of the way. Can turn things around.",
